@menu = http://localhost:5101
@orders = http://localhost:5102
@payments = http://localhost:5103

### Run individual requests in order, not the entire file at once.
### Every checkout POST creates a NEW order. Repeating the exact payment replay is safe.
### Normal simulation: SIMULATE_DECLINE=false, PAYMENT_DELAY_MS=0; see docs/classroom-demo.md.
GET {{menu}}/api/menu

### 1. Create a dedicated sample product; avoids editing existing café products (201).
# @name lectureItem
POST {{menu}}/api/menu
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Classroom Special",
  "description": "An illustrative product for the architecture demonstration.",
  "category": "Other Drinks",
  "price": 3.25,
  "isAvailable": true
}

### 2. Server controls price/status/name: total must be 6.50 and status Paid (201).
### Extra unitPrice, itemName, totalAmount and status are ignored.
# @name lectureOrder
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Classroom Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Dining Dollars",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": {{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}, "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 0.01, "itemName": "Forged name" }],
  "totalAmount": 0.02,
  "status": "Completed"
}

### 3. Retrieve the order without creating another (200).
GET {{orders}}/api/orders/{{lectureOrder.response.body.$.order.orderId}}

### 4. Retrieve the authoritative payment record (200).
# @name lecturePayment
GET {{payments}}/api/payments/order/{{lectureOrder.response.body.$.order.orderId}}

### 5. Replay EXACT payment inputs: 200, same payment ID, no second record.
POST {{payments}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{lecturePayment.response.body.$.orderId}},
  "requestId": "{{lecturePayment.response.body.$.requestId}}",
  "amount": {{lecturePayment.response.body.$.amount}},
  "paymentMethod": "{{lecturePayment.response.body.$.paymentMethod}}"
}

### 6. Conflicting amount with the same key/order: 409, no new payment.
POST {{payments}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{lecturePayment.response.body.$.orderId}},
  "requestId": "{{lecturePayment.response.body.$.requestId}}",
  "amount": 0.01,
  "paymentMethod": "{{lecturePayment.response.body.$.paymentMethod}}"
}

### 7. Change the dedicated menu product (200).
PUT {{menu}}/api/menu/{{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Classroom Special",
  "description": "The menu has changed; existing order history should not.",
  "category": "Other Drinks",
  "price": 4.00,
  "isAvailable": true
}

### 8. History still says Classroom Special, unitPrice 3.25, totalAmount 6.50 (200).
GET {{orders}}/api/orders/{{lectureOrder.response.body.$.order.orderId}}

### 9. Invalid input: 400, no new order or payment.
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Invalid Quantity Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Credit Card",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": {{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}, "quantity": 0 }]
}

### 10. ONLY after docker compose stop menu: 503 with NO saved order ID.
### Start menu again before continuing. Repeating after recovery creates a new order.
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Menu Outage Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Credit Card",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": {{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### 11. ONLY after enabling the decline mode: 402 with a saved Pending order.
# @name declinedOrder
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Decline Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Credit Card",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": {{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### 12. Pending cannot be marked Paid by staff (409).
PUT {{orders}}/api/orders/{{declinedOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Paid" }

### 13. ONLY with decline false and post-commit delay 7000 ms: 503, payment Unknown.
### Keep its saved orderId. Do not POST checkout again to check progress.
# @name lateOrder
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Late Response Demo",
  "paymentMethod": "Dining Dollars",
  "items": [{ "menuItemId": {{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}, "quantity": 1 }]
}

### 14. Payment is Succeeded even though checkout timed out (200).
GET {{payments}}/api/payments/order/{{lateOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### 15. Reconciliation marks Paid using that SAME payment record (200).
POST {{orders}}/api/orders/{{lateOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}/payment/reconcile

### 16. Optional cleanup: remove only the product created in step 1 (204).
### Its saved order snapshots and payment history remain intact.
DELETE {{menu}}/api/menu/{{lectureItem.response.body.$.menuItemId}}
